ger Sewing Machine Co and Pilkington‟s.449 An observer of many of the schemes \nreckoned that they often experienced a 60% loss of recruits.450 Certainly the companies \nneeded to fine-tune their procedures but, perhaps, an apparent paradox offers an \nexplanation. On the one hand companies complained about a lack of calibre in \ncandidates and careers advisers claimed that demand was „insistent and beyond the \n                                                 \n443 Williams, Careers for Our Sons (1914), 544. \n444 Keeble, The Ability to Manage (1992), 94. \n445 Walls E, The School Calendar, Vol. I, No.1 (September 1921), 12. \n446 Rubie, Round Pegs (1935), 218. \n447 Reader, Imperial Chemical Industries (2 Vols., 1975), ii, 76; APTB 14/13 piece 82 (Oriental Line). \n448 Tennyson, Stars and Markets (1957), 181; APTB 10/4 179 (Tootal Broadhurst Lee). \n449 APTB 10/4 155, 150 (Hedleys); APTB 14/13 piece 103 (Singer Sewing Machine Co). \n450 Transcript of Conference, FBI/200/F/3/T1/197 (1948), 32. \n \n116--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow Glass Changed the World | 9783642281822, 9783642281839 | VitalSource (https://www.vitalsource.com/products/how-glass-changed-the-world-seth-c-rasmussen-v9783642281839)\nciteturn16search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; \n\n  * Image: Cover image: How Glass Changed the World 9783642281822\n\n# How Glass Changed the World\n\n## The History and Chemistry of Glass from Antiquity to the 13th Century\n\n  * Author(s) Seth C. Rasmussen\n\n  * Publisher Published by Springer Copyright © 2012\n  * ## Print ISBN: 9783642281822\n\n\"ISBN-13 9783642281822\"\n  * Format Reflowable Layout\n\n  * Available from $ 24.00 USD\nSKU: 9783642281839R30\n\n  *   * ## eBook\n\n## eText ISBN:9783642281839\n\n[Input]30 Days\n\n$24.00\n\n[Input]60 Days\n\n$32.00\n\n[Input]90 Days\n\n$40.00\n\n[Input]120 Days\n\n$48.00\n\n[Input]180 Days\n\n$52.00\n\n[Input]Lifetime\n\n$79.99\n\neTextbook LicenseImageO